msgstr "`qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.40 or later (`pip install qiskit-ibm-runtime`)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Device Benchmarking, which also installs [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) (`pip install git+https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking.git`)\n"
msgstr "Qiskit Device Benchmarking, yang juga memasang [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) (`pip install git+https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking.git`)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import the required libraries.\n"
msgstr "Import pustaka yang diperlukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The characterization suite builds several experiments, submits multiple jobs, and fits the results. This process can take a few minutes in total. Enable INFO-level logging so that each stage prints its progress as it runs.\n"
msgstr "Suite pencirian membina beberapa eksperimen, menghantar berbilang job, dan memadankan keputusan. Proses ini boleh mengambil masa beberapa minit secara keseluruhan. Aktifkan log tahap INFO supaya setiap peringkat mencetak kemajuannya semasa ia berjalan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator berskala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial does not include a simulator example. The workflow measures the physical imperfections of a specific device: how quickly its qubits relax and dephase, and how often its gates and readout fail. An ideal simulator has none of these imperfections, so there is nothing to characterize. If you attach a synthetic noise model to a fake backend, the experiments only recover the values that you put in the model. For that reason, this tutorial proceeds directly to hardware, in the four steps of a Qiskit pattern.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini tidak mengandungi contoh simulator. Aliran kerja ini mengukur kecacatan fizikal sesuatu peranti tertentu: seberapa cepat qubitnya mengendur dan menyahfasa, dan seberapa kerap gate serta bacaannya gagal. Simulator ideal tidak mempunyai sebarang kecacatan ini, jadi tiada apa untuk dicirikan. Jika anda melampirkan model hingar sintetik kepada backend palsu, eksperimen hanya akan memulihkan nilai yang anda masukkan ke dalam model. Atas sebab itu, tutorial ini terus ke perkakasan, dalam empat langkah corak Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perkakasan berskala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Memetakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this workflow, the \"problem\" is the device itself. The classical inputs are the QPU that you want to characterize and the list of properties to measure. The quantum experiments are the characterization circuits that the utility generates from these inputs.\n"
msgstr "Dalam aliran kerja ini, \"masalah\" ialah peranti itu sendiri. Input klasik ialah QPU yang anda mahu cirikan dan senarai sifat yang hendak diukur. Eksperimen kuantum ialah litar pencirian yang dijana oleh utiliti daripada input ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, select the least-busy available QPU with a minimum of 120 qubits. The results in this tutorial were collected on `ibm_boston`, a Heron r3 processor, on 6 October 2026.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, pilih QPU yang tersedia dan paling kurang sibuk dengan sekurang-kurangnya 120 qubit. Keputusan dalam tutorial ini dikumpulkan pada `ibm_boston`, pemproses Heron r3, pada 6 Oktober 2026.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, choose which properties to measure. You can pass any subset of the following experiments:\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, pilih sifat mana yang hendak diukur. Anda boleh menghantar mana-mana subset eksperimen berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`readout`: SPAM (state preparation and measurement) experiment\n"
msgstr "`readout`: eksperimen SPAM (penyediaan dan pengukuran keadaan)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_1q`: isolated single-qubit randomized benchmarking\n"
msgstr "`rb_1q`: penanda aras rawak satu-qubit terasing\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_2q`: simultaneous two-qubit randomized benchmarking from a layer fidelity experiment\n"
msgstr "`rb_2q`: penanda aras rawak dua-qubit serentak daripada eksperimen kesetiaan lapisan\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t2`: $T_2$ Hahn echo experiment (a single echo by default)\n"
msgstr "`t2`: eksperimen gema Hahn $T_2$ (satu gema secara lalai)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t1`: $T_1$ relaxation experiment\n"
msgstr "`t1`: eksperimen relaksasi $T_1$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the full suite to characterize the device completely. To save QPU time, remove the entries for any properties that you do not need.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan suite penuh untuk mencirikan peranti sepenuhnya. Untuk menjimatkan masa QPU, buang entri bagi sebarang ciri yang tidak anda perlukan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Mengoptimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In most tutorials, this step is where you transpile your circuits. In this tutorial, `BackendCharacterization` handles transpilation internally. It builds the experiment circuits directly in the native gates of the device, runs the single-qubit experiments on all qubits in parallel, and schedules the two-qubit benchmarking over disjoint layers of the coupling map, so that a small number of jobs cover the entire device. Because of this parallelization, the whole suite uses only about 70 seconds of QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kebanyakan tutorial, langkah ini ialah tempat anda mentranspil litar anda. Dalam tutorial ini, `BackendCharacterization` mengendalikan transpilasi secara dalaman. Ia membina litar eksperimen terus dalam gate asli peranti, menjalankan eksperimen satu-qubit pada semua qubit secara selari, dan menjadualkan penanda aras dua-qubit merentasi lapisan berasingan peta gandingan, supaya sebilangan kecil job meliputi keseluruhan peranti. Disebabkan penyelarian ini, keseluruhan suite hanya menggunakan kira-kira 70 saat masa QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize the class that manages the workflow:\n"
msgstr "Mulakan kelas yang menguruskan aliran kerja:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Melaksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `run_experiments` method builds the circuits and submits them as [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) jobs. Run it inside a [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) context so that the jobs are scheduled together on the QPU. The method returns after it submits all of the jobs. You can also run the method outside a `Batch` or inside a `Session`.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `run_experiments` membina litar dan menghantarnya sebagai job [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler). Jalankannya di dalam konteks [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) supaya job dijadualkan bersama pada QPU. Kaedah ini kembali selepas ia menghantar semua job. Anda juga boleh menjalankan kaedah ini di luar `Batch` atau di dalam `Session`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You might see a warning that a backend was passed while a session context manager is open. This warning is expected, and you can safely ignore it. The layer fidelity experiment might also warn that it does not use the optional `xslow` gate. You can ignore this warning too, because the experiment uses supported standard single-qubit gates.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Anda mungkin melihat amaran bahawa backend dihantar semasa pengurus konteks session dibuka. Amaran ini dijangka, dan anda boleh mengabaikannya dengan selamat. Eksperimen kesetiaan lapisan mungkin juga memberi amaran bahawa ia tidak menggunakan gate `xslow` pilihan. Anda boleh mengabaikan amaran ini juga, kerana eksperimen menggunakan gate satu-qubit standard yang disokong.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method returns the submitted jobs as a dictionary with one entry per experiment. Use this dictionary to track the jobs on the [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](/guides/monitor-job) or to debug them.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah ini mengembalikan job yang dihantar sebagai kamus dengan satu entri bagi setiap eksperimen. Gunakan kamus ini untuk menjejak job pada [papan pemuka IBM Quantum Platform](/guides/monitor-job) atau untuk menyahpepijatnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Memproses pasca dan mengembalikan keputusan dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the results {#analyze-the-results}"
msgstr "Analisis keputusan {#analyze-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `analyze_results` method waits for the jobs to finish and then processes the measurement data. It fits exponential decays to the $T_1$ and $T_2$ data, fits survival-probability decays to the RB data, and computes assignment matrices for readout. It returns a dictionary of *error maps*, with one entry per measured property. Each error map assigns a measured value to each qubit (or qubit pair).\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `analyze_results` menunggu job selesai dan kemudian memproses data pengukuran. Ia memadankan peluruhan eksponen kepada data $T_1$ dan $T_2$, memadankan peluruhan kebarangkalian kemandirian kepada data RB, dan mengira matriks penugasan untuk bacaan. Ia mengembalikan kamus *peta ralat*, dengan satu entri bagi setiap sifat yang diukur. Setiap peta ralat memberikan nilai terukur kepada setiap qubit (atau pasangan qubit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maps cover readout error, the single-qubit `x` and `sx` gate errors, the layered two-qubit errors (`lf_error_map`, from the layer fidelity experiment), and the $T_1$ and $T_2$ times in seconds.\n"
msgstr "Peta tersebut meliputi ralat bacaan, ralat gate `x` dan `sx` satu-qubit, ralat dua-qubit berlapis (`lf_error_map`, daripada eksperimen kesetiaan lapisan), dan masa $T_1$ dan $T_2$ dalam saat.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the backend properties {#update-the-backend-properties}"
msgstr "Kemas kini sifat backend {#update-the-backend-properties}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `update_backend` method writes the measured values into the properties of a copy of the backend and returns the copy. The original `backend` object keeps the reported calibration data, so that you can compare the two sets of properties, as shown in the next section. This update applies only to your Python session. It does not change anything on the device or for other users.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `update_backend` menulis nilai terukur ke dalam ciri salinan backend dan mengembalikan salinan tersebut. Objek `backend` asal mengekalkan data kalibrasi yang dilaporkan, supaya anda dapat membandingkan kedua-dua set ciri, seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam bahagian seterusnya. Kemas kini ini hanya terpakai pada session Python anda. Ia tidak mengubah apa-apa pada peranti atau untuk pengguna lain.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the measured properties against the reported ones {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"
msgstr "Bandingkan sifat terukur berbanding yang dilaporkan {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, plot the measured real-time properties against the values that the backend reports. In each panel, the qubits (or qubit pairs) are sorted by measured value, so the measured curve is smooth by construction. The scatter of the reported values around this curve shows where the two data sets disagree. The single-qubit RB results appear in one plot, because the utility assigns the same measured error per gate to both the `x` and `sx` gates. The axis limits are based on most of the data, so that a few extreme outliers do not compress the plots. An annotation on each plot counts any points that fall outside the range. To set the limits yourself, pass the `ylim` argument.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, plotkan ciri masa nyata yang diukur berbanding nilai yang dilaporkan oleh backend. Dalam setiap panel, qubit (atau pasangan qubit) disusun mengikut nilai terukur, jadi lengkung terukur adalah licin secara pembinaan. Serakan nilai yang dilaporkan di sekitar lengkung ini menunjukkan di mana kedua-dua set data tidak sepadan. Keputusan RB satu-qubit dipaparkan dalam satu plot, kerana utiliti memberikan ralat terukur yang sama bagi setiap gate kepada kedua-dua gate `x` dan `sx`. Had paksi berdasarkan kebanyakan data, supaya beberapa outlier ekstrem tidak memampatkan plot. Anotasi pada setiap plot mengira sebarang titik yang jatuh di luar julat. Untuk menetapkan had sendiri, hantar argumen `ylim`.\n"

