# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read these plots carefully, because not every gap between the two curves means that the device has drifted:\n"
msgstr "Baca plot ini dengan teliti, kerana bukan setiap jurang antara kedua-dua lengkung bermakna peranti telah hanyut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Readout and single-qubit errors**: The measured values track the reported ones for most qubits, but for a few qubits the reported value is far from the measured curve. These localized disagreements can reflect the drift that this workflow is designed to detect.\n"
msgstr "**Ralat bacaan dan satu-qubit**: Nilai terukur mengikuti nilai yang dilaporkan bagi kebanyakan qubit, tetapi bagi segelintir qubit nilai yang dilaporkan jauh daripada lengkung terukur. Ketidaksepakatan setempat ini boleh mencerminkan hanyutan yang aliran kerja ini direka untuk dikesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$**: The two data sets scatter around each other with no systematic offset, which is consistent with natural fluctuation of $T_1$ over time.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$**: Kedua-dua set data berserak di sekeliling satu sama lain tanpa ofset sistematik, yang konsisten dengan turun naik semula jadi $T_1$ dari semasa ke semasa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two-qubit errors**: The measured values are systematically above the reported ones. This difference is expected, because the reported values come from isolated gates, while the layer fidelity experiment runs many gates simultaneously and therefore includes crosstalk. The layered values are more relevant for deep circuits, but they are not directly comparable to the reported calibration data.\n"
msgstr "**Ralat dua-qubit**: Nilai terukur secara sistematik *lebih tinggi* daripada nilai yang dilaporkan. Ini dijangka kerana nilai yang dilaporkan datang daripada gate terasing, manakala eksperimen kesetiaan lapisan menjalankan banyak gate serentak dan oleh itu merangkumi crosstalk. Nilai berlapis lebih relevan untuk litar yang mendalam, tetapi ia tidak boleh dibandingkan secara langsung dengan data kalibrasi yang dilaporkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$**: The measured values are well below the reported ones for most qubits. As with the two-qubit errors, methodology plays a large role, which the next section examines.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$**: Nilai terukur jauh di bawah nilai yang dilaporkan bagi kebanyakan qubit. Seperti ralat dua-qubit, metodologi memainkan peranan besar, yang diteliti dalam bahagian seterusnya.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect individual experiment results {#inspect-individual-experiment-results}"
msgstr "Periksa keputusan eksperimen individu {#inspect-individual-experiment-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also inspect the raw results of the individual characterization experiments through the `experiment_data` property, which returns the underlying [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) `ExperimentData` objects. For example, the following code displays the measured $T_1$ decay curve of a single qubit. Use a curve like this one to check the quality of a fit before you rely on the value that the fit produced.\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh memeriksa keputusan mentah eksperimen pencirian individu melalui sifat `experiment_data`, yang mengembalikan objek `ExperimentData` [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) yang mendasarinya. Sebagai contoh, kod berikut memaparkan lengkung reputan $T_1$ terukur bagi satu qubit. Gunakan lengkung seperti ini untuk menyemak kualiti padanan sebelum anda bergantung pada nilai yang dihasilkan oleh padanan itu.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-28-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-28-1.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure T2 with a dynamical decoupling train {#measure-t2-with-a-dynamical-decoupling-train}"
msgstr "Ukur T2 dengan jujukan denyut penyahgandingan dinamik {#measure-t2-with-a-dynamical-decoupling-train}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, the $T_2$ experiment applies a single Hahn echo and measures all qubits in parallel. As the previous comparison plot shows, this method can produce noticeably lower $T_2$ values than the backend reports. One possible cause is the number of echoes. The reported values might come from a calibration that uses dynamical decoupling, which suppresses low-frequency noise. To test this hypothesis, run a $T_2$-only characterization with a larger value of `t2_num_echoes`, which applies a CPMG-style train of echo pulses. In both cases, the delays represent the total free-evolution time, so the fitted $T_2$ values are directly comparable to the single-echo results.\n"
msgstr "Secara lalai, eksperimen $T_2$ menggunakan satu gema Hahn dan mengukur semua qubit secara selari. Seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh plot perbandingan sebelum ini, kaedah ini boleh menghasilkan nilai $T_2$ yang jauh lebih rendah daripada yang dilaporkan oleh backend. Satu punca yang mungkin ialah bilangan gema. Nilai yang dilaporkan mungkin berasal daripada kalibrasi yang menggunakan penyahgandingan dinamik, yang menekan hingar frekuensi rendah. Untuk menguji hipotesis ini, jalankan pencirian $T_2$ sahaja dengan nilai `t2_num_echoes` yang lebih besar, yang menggunakan jujukan denyut gema bergaya CPMG. Dalam kedua-dua kes, kelewatan mewakili jumlah masa evolusi bebas, jadi nilai $T_2$ yang dipadankan boleh dibandingkan secara langsung dengan keputusan gema tunggal.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-31-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-31-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this run, the extra echoes barely changed the result. The 8-echo median (77 &micro;s) is close to the single-echo median (75 &micro;s), and both remain far below the reported median (300 &micro;s). The number of echoes alone does not explain this gap. Other methodological differences also contribute, such as details of the calibration procedure, and measurement of all qubits in parallel instead of in isolation.\n"
msgstr "Dalam larian ini, gema tambahan hampir tidak mengubah keputusan. Median 8-gema (77 &micro;s) hampir sama dengan median gema tunggal (75 &micro;s), dan kedua-duanya kekal jauh lebih rendah daripada median yang dilaporkan (300 &micro;s). Bilangan gema sahaja tidak menjelaskan jurang ini. Perbezaan metodologi lain juga menyumbang, seperti perincian prosedur kalibrasi, dan pengukuran semua qubit secara selari dan bukannya secara terasing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, compare $T_2$ values (and layered two-qubit errors) across methodologies with care. The refreshed values are a self-consistent snapshot, taken under conditions close to those of a real workload. These values are well suited to compare qubits with each other or to track a device over time. A gap relative to the reported calibration data, however, is not automatically evidence of drift.\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, bandingkan nilai $T_2$ (dan ralat dua-qubit berlapis) merentasi metodologi dengan berhati-hati. Nilai yang disegarkan ialah gambaran konsisten-diri, diambil di bawah keadaan yang hampir dengan keadaan beban kerja sebenar. Nilai ini sesuai untuk membandingkan qubit antara satu sama lain atau menjejak peranti dari semasa ke semasa. Namun, jurang berbanding data penentukuran yang dilaporkan bukanlah secara automatik bukti hanyutan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run steps 1–4 in a single call {#run-steps-14-in-a-single-call}"
msgstr "Jalankan langkah 1–4 dalam satu panggilan {#run-steps-14-in-a-single-call}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For routine use, you rarely need the intermediate results. The `run_and_update` method combines the previous steps (build, submit, fit, and update) into a single call that returns the refreshed backend. It accepts the same `experiments` list and forwards options such as `t2_num_echoes`. You can also wrap it in a `Batch` or `Session` context.\n"
msgstr "Untuk kegunaan rutin, anda jarang memerlukan keputusan pertengahan. Kaedah `run_and_update` menggabungkan langkah-langkah sebelumnya (membina, menghantar, memadankan, dan mengemas kini) ke dalam satu panggilan yang mengembalikan backend yang disegarkan. Ia menerima senarai `experiments` yang sama dan meneruskan pilihan seperti `t2_num_echoes`. Anda juga boleh membalutnya dalam konteks `Batch` atau `Session`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The following cell does not return until all jobs and post-processing are complete.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sel berikut tidak akan kembali sehingga semua job dan pemprosesan pasca selesai.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The refreshed `backend_updated` object is ready for the GHZ comparison in the next section. Refresh the properties close to execution time to reduce the effect of further device drift.\n"
msgstr "Objek `backend_updated` yang disegarkan sedia untuk perbandingan GHZ dalam bahagian seterusnya. Segarkan sifat-sifat tersebut menghampiri masa pelaksanaan untuk mengurangkan kesan hanyutan peranti selanjutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use refreshed properties for qubit selection {#use-refreshed-properties-for-qubit-selection}"
msgstr "Gunakan sifat yang disegarkan untuk pemilihan qubit {#use-refreshed-properties-for-qubit-selection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This optional example completes the workflow. It checks whether the refreshed properties lead to better circuit results. It compiles the same circuits twice, once with the reported properties and once with the refreshed properties. Then it runs both versions and compares their outputs. This example uses the `backend` and `backend_updated` objects from the previous sections, and it submits additional work to the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Contoh pilihan ini melengkapkan aliran kerja. Ia menyemak sama ada sifat yang disegarkan menghasilkan keputusan litar yang lebih baik. Ia menyusun litar yang sama dua kali, sekali dengan sifat yang dilaporkan dan sekali dengan sifat yang disegarkan. Kemudian ia menjalankan kedua-dua versi dan membandingkan outputnya. Contoh ini menggunakan objek `backend` dan `backend_updated` daripada bahagian sebelumnya, dan ia menghantar kerja tambahan kepada QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the comparison circuits {#build-the-comparison-circuits}"
msgstr "Bina litar perbandingan {#build-the-comparison-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare an $n$-qubit Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) state with a Hadamard gate followed by a chain of CNOT gates, and measure every qubit. Ideally, the outcomes $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ and $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$ each have probability 0.5. Because you measure every qubit, an error on any qubit in the chain, including a readout error, reduces the probability of the ideal outcomes. The measured outputs are therefore sensitive to the physical qubits that the transpiler selects.\n"
msgstr "Sediakan keadaan Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) $n$-qubit dengan gate Hadamard diikuti rantaian gate CNOT, dan ukur setiap qubit. Secara ideal, hasil $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$ masing-masing mempunyai kebarangkalian 0.5. Oleh kerana anda mengukur setiap qubit, ralat pada mana-mana qubit dalam rantaian, termasuk ralat bacaan, mengurangkan kebarangkalian hasil yang ideal. Output yang diukur oleh itu sensitif terhadap qubit fizikal yang dipilih oleh Transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refreshed properties tend to matter most at moderate sizes, where the transpiler can choose from many candidate qubit chains. Very large circuits use most of the device, so the transpiler has little room to avoid poorly performing qubits. To save QPU time, reduce the list of circuit sizes.\n"
msgstr "Sifat yang disegarkan cenderung paling penting pada saiz sederhana, apabila Transpiler boleh memilih daripada banyak rantaian qubit calon. Litar yang sangat besar menggunakan sebahagian besar peranti, jadi Transpiler mempunyai sedikit ruang untuk mengelakkan qubit yang berprestasi buruk. Untuk menjimatkan masa QPU, kurangkan senarai saiz litar.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-circuits-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-circuits-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile with reported and refreshed properties {#transpile-with-reported-and-refreshed-properties}"
msgstr "Transpile dengan sifat yang dilaporkan dan disegarkan {#transpile-with-reported-and-refreshed-properties}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The transpiler uses a `Target` to choose physical qubits and native instructions. If you update only the backend properties, an existing target can remain unchanged. Instead, copy the original target and explicitly apply the refreshed errors and coherence times to the copy. The copy keeps the original instruction durations and connectivity. If a coherence time is unavailable for a qubit, keep its existing target value.\n"
msgstr "Transpiler menggunakan `Target` untuk memilih qubit fizikal dan arahan asli. Jika anda hanya mengemas kini sifat backend, target sedia ada boleh kekal tidak berubah. Sebaliknya, salin target asal dan gunakan ralat serta masa koheren yang disegarkan secara eksplisit pada salinan tersebut. Salinan itu mengekalkan tempoh arahan dan kesambungan asal. Jika masa koheren tidak tersedia untuk sesuatu qubit, kekalkan nilai target sedia adanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A reported error of 1 means that the error is undefined, because benchmarking of that qubit or gate has not succeeded for several days, and the value is outdated (see [QPU information](/guides/qpu-information)). This value does not necessarily mean that the gate is not working, but you should treat the gate with caution. A single characterization run can still fit a low error for such a gate, so that the gate appears to be one of the best on the device. To be cautious, keep those entries at their reported value so that the transpiler continues to avoid them.\n"
msgstr "Ralat yang dilaporkan bernilai 1 bermaksud ralat itu tidak ditakrifkan, kerana penanda aras bagi qubit atau gate tersebut tidak berjaya selama beberapa hari, dan nilainya sudah lapuk (lihat [Maklumat QPU](/guides/qpu-information)). Nilai ini tidak semestinya bermaksud gate tersebut tidak berfungsi, tetapi anda harus berhati-hati dengan gate tersebut. Satu larian pencirian tunggal masih boleh memadankan ralat rendah untuk gate sedemikian, sehingga gate itu kelihatan seperti salah satu yang terbaik pada peranti. Untuk berhati-hati, kekalkan entri tersebut pada nilai yang dilaporkan supaya Transpiler terus mengelakkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the same optimization level and random seed for both compilations so that the comparison controls for transpiler randomness.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan tahap pengoptimuman dan benih rawak yang sama untuk kedua-dua kompilasi supaya perbandingan mengawal kerawakan Transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you run the circuits, check how many physical qubits each refreshed layout changes. If the two compilations select the same qubits, the refreshed properties cannot make a difference for that circuit.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum anda menjalankan litar, semak berapa banyak qubit fizikal yang diubah oleh setiap susun atur yang disegarkan. Jika kedua-dua kompilasi memilih qubit yang sama, sifat yang disegarkan tidak dapat membuat perbezaan untuk litar tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute both sets of circuits {#execute-both-sets-of-circuits}"
msgstr "Laksanakan kedua-dua set litar {#execute-both-sets-of-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run both versions on the same QPU, with the same shot count and error suppression settings. Interleave the reported and refreshed versions in the submission, and repeat the comparison three times to observe the variation between trials. The order of submission does not guarantee the order of execution, and interleaving does not eliminate drift.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan kedua-dua versi pada QPU yang sama, dengan bilangan tembakan dan tetapan penindasan ralat yang sama. Selang-selikan versi yang dilaporkan dan yang disegarkan dalam penghantaran, dan ulang perbandingan tiga kali untuk memerhati variasi antara percubaan. Urutan penghantaran tidak menjamin urutan pelaksanaan, dan penyelang-selian tidak menghapuskan hanyutan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the output distributions {#compare-the-output-distributions}"
msgstr "Bandingkan taburan output {#compare-the-output-distributions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the Hellinger fidelity between each measured distribution and the ideal GHZ distribution. A value of 1 means that the distributions match. This metric measures agreement only in the computational basis. It does not measure the coherence between $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ and $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$, so it is an upper bound on the GHZ state fidelity, not a certificate of entanglement.\n"
msgstr "Kira kesetiaan Hellinger antara setiap taburan yang diukur dengan taburan GHZ ideal. Nilai 1 bermaksud taburan tersebut sepadan. Metrik ini hanya mengukur persetujuan dalam asas pengiraan. Ia tidak mengukur koheren antara $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$, jadi ia ialah had atas bagi kesetiaan keadaan GHZ, bukan sijil belitan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plot shows the mean across trials. The error bars indicate one standard deviation.\n"
msgstr "Plot menunjukkan purata merentasi percubaan. Palang ralat menunjukkan satu sisihan piawai.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-results-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-results-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this run, the refreshed properties changed some or all of the selected qubits at every size, and the refreshed layouts gave a higher mean fidelity for seven of the eight GHZ states. The largest gain was for the 25-qubit state, where the mean fidelity increased from 0.629 to 0.694. The refreshed layout scored higher in every trial for the 5-, 10-, 20-, 25-, 35-, and 40-qubit states. Not every size improved. For the 15-qubit state, the refreshed layout was slightly worse (0.813 compared with 0.821). For the 30-qubit state, the difference (0.596 compared with 0.591) is within the variation between trials.\n"
msgstr "Dalam larian ini, sifat yang disegarkan mengubah sebahagian atau semua qubit yang dipilih pada setiap saiz, dan susun atur yang disegarkan memberikan purata kesetiaan yang lebih tinggi bagi tujuh daripada lapan keadaan GHZ. Peningkatan terbesar ialah untuk keadaan 25-qubit, apabila purata kesetiaan meningkat daripada 0.629 kepada 0.694. Susun atur yang disegarkan mencatat skor lebih tinggi dalam setiap percubaan bagi keadaan 5-, 10-, 20-, 25-, 35-, dan 40-qubit. Tidak semua saiz bertambah baik. Untuk keadaan 15-qubit, susun atur yang disegarkan sedikit lebih teruk (0.813 berbanding 0.821). Untuk keadaan 30-qubit, perbezaan (0.596 berbanding 0.591) berada dalam lingkungan variasi antara percubaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refreshed properties do not guarantee better results. The benefit depends on how far the device has drifted since its last calibration. Also, the characterization is itself a noisy snapshot. The transpiler can select a qubit or gate that happens to measure well, even if that qubit or gate does not perform better. Shot noise, further drift between characterization and execution, and differences in characterization methodology also affect the comparison. Use the measured change and its variation to decide whether refreshed properties are useful for your workload.\n"
msgstr "Sifat yang disegarkan tidak menjamin keputusan yang lebih baik. Manfaatnya bergantung pada sejauh mana peranti telah hanyut sejak penentukuran terakhirnya. Selain itu, pencirian itu sendiri ialah gambaran yang berhingar. Transpiler boleh memilih qubit atau gate yang kebetulan diukur dengan baik, walaupun qubit atau gate itu tidak berprestasi lebih baik. Hingar tembakan, hanyutan selanjutnya antara pencirian dan pelaksanaan, serta perbezaan dalam metodologi pencirian juga menjejaskan perbandingan. Gunakan perubahan yang diukur dan variasinya untuk memutuskan sama ada sifat yang disegarkan berguna untuk beban kerja anda.\n"

